  "headline": "Anuradhapura & Polonnaruwa: Sacred Stupas, Royal Palaces & Colossal Stone Buddhas",
  "description": "Anuradhapura ruled for more than a thousand years: its great stupas rival the pyramids in scale and the Sri Maha Bodhi, grown from a cutting of the Buddha’s own tree, is still venerated daily. Polonnaruwa, the medieval capital, is more compact — palaces, audience halls and the sublime rock-cut Buddhas of Gal Vihara.\n\nI explore both early or late in the day, by vintage bicycle where the paths allow, with the stories that bring the stones back to life.",
